<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Illinois</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Illinois is a state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midwestern-united-states">Midwestern United States</a>, lying between Lake Michigan and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> river, with Springfield as its capital and Chicago as its largest city. Named after the Illinois Confederation, it was part of the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois-country">Illinois Country</a> before passing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1763 and then to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, which admitted it as a state in 1818. In the 1840s Nauvoo, Illinois, was the centre of the Latter-day Saints.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/illinois.jpg" alt="Illinois" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Denelson83 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Illinois.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
